      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-54414",
      ":question/problem": "An airplane is flying over the Caribbean Sea. En route to its destination, it locates a ship on the sea $4km$ away. At the same time, it locates a second ship $5km$ away. The distance between the ships is $7km$.\nDetermine the angle formed between the first ship, the airplane, and the second ship. Round your answer to one decimal place.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
